        <caption>BeModelDiagnosticReportDiabetes</caption>
        <thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Description</th><th>Relation</th><th>Glossary concept</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>BeModelDiagnosticReportDiabetes.BusinessIdentifier</td><td>Report identifier for the internal supplier's business.</td><td>equivalent</td><td><a href="https://caresets.github.io/en/glossary_clinical.html#BusinessIdentifier">BusinessIdentifier</a></td></tr>
          <tr><td>BeModelDiagnosticReportDiabetes.Category</td><td>Category of the report. According to ref. 8, it would be appropriate to consider setting the cardinality of the Catgory field to 1..* and to add to this report the values: 4311000179106 |Chemical pathology report (record artifact) and 408475000 |Diabetic medicine (qualifier value). 394583002 |Endocrinology (qualifier value) of the report. Look at VS_DiagRep_Category.</td><td>equivalent</td><td><a href="https://caresets.github.io/en/glossary_clinical.html#Category">Category</a></td></tr>
          <tr><td>BeModelDiagnosticReportDiabetes.Code</td><td>Report code. In the diabetes project framework, it is proposed to indicate the type of procedure that leads to the production of the primary values ​​of this report. That is to say 439926003 | Ambulatory continuous glucose monitoring of interstitial tissue fluid. VS_DiagRep_Code.</td><td>equivalent</td><td><a href="https://caresets.github.io/en/glossary_clinical.html#Code">Code</a></td></tr>
          <tr><td>BeModelDiagnosticReportDiabetes.Device</td><td>Identification number assigned by INAMI to the sensor type.See VS_Diab_Device</td><td>equivalent</td><td><a href="https://caresets.github.io/en/glossary_clinical.html#UsedDevice">UsedDevice</a></td></tr>
          <tr><td>BeModelDiagnosticReportDiabetes.Note</td><td>Report comments in free text format. This element will not be provided by the producer of the report, but will be provided by the healthcare provider doing the interpretation.</td><td>equivalent</td><td><a href="https://caresets.github.io/en/glossary_clinical.html#Note">Note</a></td></tr>
          <tr><td>BeModelDiagnosticReportDiabetes.Patient</td><td>We refer to the patient, subject of the report, by his unique identifier.This identifier is preferably the patient's national register number (NISS). In some cases, another unique identifier may be allowed.</td><td>equivalent</td><td><a href="https://caresets.github.io/en/glossary_clinical.html#Patient">Patient</a></td></tr>
          <tr><td>BeModelDiagnosticReportDiabetes.Performer</td><td>We refer to the service provider or organization that collects the observations and produces the report. [2]The unique identifier of each natural person is the NISS, while for each organization the company number serves as the unique identifier.For the Diabetes Diagnostic Report, it is: “performer = recorder.»</td><td>equivalent</td><td><a href="https://caresets.github.io/en/glossary_clinical.html#Performer">Performer</a></td></tr>
          <tr><td>BeModelDiagnosticReportDiabetes.RecordedDate</td><td>Date the report was produced.</td><td>equivalent</td><td><a href="https://caresets.github.io/en/glossary_clinical.html#RecordedDate">RecordedDate</a></td></tr>
          <tr><td>BeModelDiagnosticReportDiabetes.Recorder</td><td>This refers to the service provider or organization that encodes the information.[1] The unique identifier for each natural person is the NISS, while for each organization the business number serves as the unique identifier.</td><td>equivalent</td><td><a href="https://caresets.github.io/en/glossary_clinical.html#Recorder">Recorder</a></td></tr>
          <tr><td>BeModelDiagnosticReportDiabetes.Status</td><td>Report status. By default it is “Final”. Value according to the business rule on “% Data Captured” see VS_DiagRep_Status</td><td>equivalent</td><td><a href="https://caresets.github.io/en/glossary_clinical.html#Status">Status</a></td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
